<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Scott asked for a same-day visit for vomiting and diarrhea that began a day and a half ago, the evening after a crowded fundraising dinner; two other guests have told him they are ill too. He vomited five times on the first night and has had six or seven watery stools a day since, with cramping before each. He has no blood or black stool, no severe or constant abdominal pain, and the vomiting stopped this morning. He feels lightheaded when he stands. He has felt hot but has no rigors. He is passing less urine. He has kept down only small sips of water. He took his losartan yesterday morning and this morning. He started losartan two weeks ago and has not missed a dose. He has had no recent travel abroad, antibiotics, or hospital stay. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Onset</td><td>A day and a half ago, the evening after a crowded dinner</td></tr><tr><td>Location</td><td>Cramping around the navel before each stool</td></tr><tr><td>Duration</td><td>About 36 hours</td></tr><tr><td>Character</td><td>Watery diarrhea without blood; vomiting, now stopped</td></tr><tr><td>Severity</td><td>Six or seven stools a day; lightheaded on standing</td></tr><tr><td>Timing</td><td>Vomiting the first night; diarrhea continuing</td></tr><tr><td>Context</td><td>Others at the same dinner ill; started losartan two weeks ago</td></tr><tr><td>Modifying factors</td><td>Small sips of water kept down since this morning</td></tr><tr><td>Associated signs and symptoms</td><td>Felt hot; less urine; no blood in the stool, no severe pain</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

