<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Acute viral gastroenteritis with mild dehydration (A08.4)</content>. Acute watery diarrhea after vomiting, with similar illness in others at the same meal, most likely viral. Mild dehydration with a postural rise in pulse. No blood in the stool, no high fever and no severe pain, so stool testing and antibiotics are not needed. Creatinine 1.16 mg/dL, up from 0.92 at intake (eGFR 81), with sodium 137 and potassium 3.8 mmol/L: a modest rise from losing fluid while taking an angiotensin receptor blocker, not kidney injury. [S]<list><item>Oral rehydration solution, small amounts often, aiming for at least 2 to 3 liters today.</item><item>Hold losartan under the sick-day rule until he is eating and drinking normally for 24 hours, then restart at the same dose.</item><item>Loperamide is acceptable for comfort if there is no fever above 38.5 °C and no blood in the stool.</item><item>Hand hygiene and no food preparation for others until 48 hours after the last symptoms.</item><item>Return the same day for blood in the stool, vomiting that stops all fluids, fainting, very little urine, or symptoms lasting more than a week.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Hypertension on losartan (I10)</content>. Blood pressure low for him today with dehydration; the sick-day rule applies. [S]<list><item>Restart losartan when well; repeat electrolytes and creatinine at the pre-departure visit in three weeks.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: 2025 AHA/ACC/AANP/AAPA/ABC/ACCP/ACPM/AGS/AMA/ASPC/NMA/PCNA/SGIM Guideline for the Prevention, Detection, Evaluation and Management of High Blood Pressure in Adults (Jones DW, et al. Circulation 2025;152(11):e114-e218) (2025); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, hypertension monograph (2026); 2017 Infectious Diseases Society of America Clinical Practice Guidelines for the Diagnosis and Management of Infectious Diarrhea (Shane AL, et al. Clin Infect Dis 2017;65(12):e45-e80) (2017)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Telephone check in two days. Pre-departure review in three weeks, as scheduled, with electrolytes and creatinine. Next scheduled visit 2026-05-26: pre-departure review: electrolytes on losartan, blood pressure, mental health, and the expedition medical plan. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
